244	/// Runs sub-agents concurrently (cooperative `futures::stream::select_all` — core
245	/// has no tokio runtime), interleaving their events live. Each branch is keyed;
246	/// on completion its final text is written to `state[key]` (disjoint keys → safe).
247	///
248	/// `final_output` is deterministic: a synthesized terminal `MessageOutput` carrying
249	/// a sorted-key JSON object `{key: branch_output}` is emitted before the outer
250	/// `RunCompleted`. Per-branch results are addressed individually via `state[key]`.
251	/// Failure is **collect-all**: child `RunFailed` events are swallowed, siblings
252	/// finish, and one aggregate `RunFailed` is emitted.
253	///
254	/// Cooperative concurrency suits IO-bound `model.invoke`; a CPU-bound branch would
255	/// starve siblings between `.await` points. This is not OS-thread parallelism.
256	pub struct ParallelAgent<Ctx> {
